From 10ca4348c9b399e0b3863af90ddef5eb5470ca63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 06:29:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda/hip: let the skinny f32 GEMM take the small tail ubatch
 too (+8.6% prefill)

0044 added a wave-tiled f32 GEMM for the shapes rocBLAS under-parallelises and
guarded it with min_cols = 32. That lower bound excluded exactly the shapes
where the vendor BLAS is worst: fewer columns means fewer output tiles means
fewer workgroups.

Any prompt longer than one physical batch ends in a short tail ubatch, and the
ranked 512-token prompt tokenises to ~534, so every request has one of 22
tokens. At M = 22 the guard rejects and 100 matmuls per pass land on
Cijk_Alik_Bljk_S_B_Bias_HA_S_SAV running on 1 to 4 workgroups of a 64 CU part:
11.49 ms of a 135.59 ms pp534 pass. The same 100 launches in this kernel are
3.21 ms.

Measured by kernel census at pp534: the rocBLAS kernel disappears entirely and
mul_mat_f32_skinny_cuda<8,8,4,false> takes its place, f32/GEMM time per pass
26.63 -> 18.30 ms.

Lowered to 8 rather than 1 so decode-shape matvecs (M = 1) stay on the
mmvf/mmvq paths rounds 17-53 tuned; measured flat between 2 and 8.

GGML_F32_SKINNY_MIN_COLS=32 restores the old threshold.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmf32-skinny.cu | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmf32-skinny.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmf32-skinny.cu
index cda1844ae..5e7773fc8 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmf32-skinny.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmf32-skinny.cu
@@ -132,7 +132,16 @@ static int mmf32_skinny_max_rows() {
 static int mmf32_skinny_min_cols() {
     static const int v = []() {
         const char * s = getenv("GGML_F32_SKINNY_MIN_COLS");
-        return s ? atoi(s) : 32;
+        // 0044 shipped this at 32, which excluded exactly the shapes where the vendor
+        // BLAS is WORST.  Fewer columns means fewer output tiles means fewer
+        // workgroups: a 22-column tail ubatch lands rocBLAS on a 1-4 workgroup
+        // Cijk_..._S_B_Bias_... on a 64 CU part, 100 launches and 11.49 ms of a
+        // 135.59 ms pp534 pass.  The same work in this kernel is 3.21 ms.
+        // Any prompt longer than one physical batch has such a tail, and the ranked
+        // 512-token prompt tokenises to ~534, so it has one every request.
+        // 8 rather than 1: decode-shape matvecs (M = 1) must stay on the mmvf/mmvq
+        // paths that rounds 17-53 tuned.  Measured flat between 2 and 8.
+        return s ? atoi(s) : 8;
     }();
     return v;
 }
